-- Regression: a POLYMORPHIC def referenced bare (unapplied) at a ground type.
-- The resolver must NOT canonicalize the poly name `myid` to `RResolved` — poly
-- defs are INLINED (`t-var-poly-instantiate`), not given a monomorphic symbol, so
-- a resolved poly name has nothing to resolve to (poly sigs live in `polys`, not
-- the import table) and the elaborator reports "unbound/unspecialized".
-- Compare: a MONO def (`incr` below) bare-referenced DOES resolve fine.
-- This was hidden by the `resolver-preserves-typing` postulate (ResolverBridge).

myid : a -> a
myid = id

useId : Int -> Int
useId = myid

incr : Int -> Int
incr = id

useIncr : Int -> Int
useIncr = incr
